{
  "schema_version": 1,
  "name": "Phaser",
  "description": "The swirling, liquid sweep: a chain of allpass filters shifts the phase of the signal by an amount that depends on frequency, and blending it with the dry signal cancels a few bands, making notches that glide up and down the spectrum. Mono or stereo; the output has as many channels as the input.\n\n- `in`: the signal.\n- `rate` (Hz): sweeps per second.\n- `depth` (0 to 1): how far the notches sweep, up to two octaves either side of `center` (at 0.5, one octave either side).\n- `center` (Hz): the middle of the sweep. The notches sit around it: with 2 notches, at about 0.4 and 2.4 times the swept frequency.\n- `notches` (2, 3, or 4): how many notches, from 4, 6, or 8 allpass stages. More notches sound denser and more pronounced. Other values wrap around (5 is 2 again).\n- `mix` (0 to 1): 0 is dry, 1 is only the phase-shifted signal (a gentle wobble, no notches); 0.5 cancels fully and gives the deepest notches.\n- `out`: the result.\n\nInside: a `pure` sine Oscillator at `rate` is mapped exponentially between `center` ÷ and × the sweep ratio (Convert turns `depth` × 24 semitones into that ratio), so the sweep is even in octaves. Each stage is an Allpass with a one-sample delay, which makes it the first-order allpass of an analog phaser stage; its `gain` sets the frequency where it shifts the phase by 90°, and for a frequency f that gain is tan(π/4 − π·f / sample rate), worked out per sample by the Math and Unary nodes (Convert of π samples to seconds gives π / sample rate, so the sweep is the same at any rate). Select picks the output after 4, 6, or 8 stages, and a Crossfade blends it with the dry input. There is no feedback control: a loop around the stages needs a Feedback node, whose block of delay would make a comb filter instead of a phaser's resonance.",
  "version": 1,
  "author": "Audio Constructor",
  "tags": [
    "modulation",
    "phaser",
    "filter",
    "allpass",
    "effect"
  ],
  "inputs": [
    {
      "name": "in",
      "type": "audio",
      "targets": [
        "11:in",
        "20:a"
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "rate",
      "type": "float",
      "unit": "hz",
      "default": 0.3,
      "range": [
        0.02,
        5.0
      ],
      "targets": [
        "5:freq"
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "depth",
      "type": "float",
      "default": 0.6,
      "range": [
        0.0,
        1.0
      ],
      "targets": [
        "1:a"
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "center",
      "type": "float",
      "unit": "hz",
      "default": 800.0,
      "range": [
        200.0,
        4000.0
      ],
      "targets": [
        "3:a",
        "4:a"
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "notches",
      "type": "int",
      "default": 2,
      "range": [
        2.0,
        4.0
      ],
      "targets": [
        "19:index"
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "mix",
      "type": "float",
      "default": 0.5,
      "range": [
        0.0,
        1.0
      ],
      "targets": [
        "20:mix"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "outputs": [
    {
      "name": "out",
      "type": "audio",
      "source": "20:out"
    }
  ],
  "graph": {
    "nodes": [
      {
        "id": "1",
        "kind": "math",
        "params": {
          "b": 24.0,
          "op": "multiply"
        },
        "ui": {
          "pos": [
            0.0,
            300.0
          ],
          "label": "Depth (st)"
        }
      },
      {
        "id": "2",
        "kind": "convert",
        "params": {
          "op": "semitones_to_ratio"
        },
        "ui": {
          "pos": [
            240.0,
            300.0
          ],
          "label": "Sweep ratio"
        }
      },
      {
